# Windows are resized with the grip in their bottom right corner. The first
# extra window lies at 32,32: 80x25 characters is a frame of 652x436, so
# its grip is at 670..682, 454..466. Pulling it 160 x 80 pixels makes the
# window 20 columns wider and 5 lines higher (812x516).
@usb kbd mouse
$ layout us
$ files /
~ in a new window
# Before: its right border at x=683 (the console's window lies behind it).
@screenshot 1920x1080 pixels 34,34=3a6ea5 683,300=1f3a5f 843,300=000000
# The pointer starts in the middle (960,540).
@mouse -284 -80
@button left down
@mouse 160 80
@button left up
$ sleep 1
# After: the border moved to x=843, the bottom one to y=547.
@screenshot 1920x1080 pixels 683,300=000000 843,300=1f3a5f 500,547=1f3a5f 500,467=000000
$ threads
~ files      (waiting|ready)
